cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KPM.jl in your research, please cite this software using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "KPM.jl: A Julia Package for Kernel Polynomial Method in Condensed Matter Physics"
authors:
  - family-names: Wu
    given-names: Ang-Kun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7018-1674"
  - family-names: Fu
    given-names: Yixing
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9470-8848"
  - family-names: Wilson
    given-names: Justin H.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6903-0417"
  - family-names: Pixley
    given-names: J. H.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3109-640X"
version: "0.1.1"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pixley-Research-Group-in-CMT/KPM.jl"
license: MPL-2.0
abstract: >-
  KPM.jl is a Julia implementation of the Kernel Polynomial Method for
  tight-binding models in condensed matter physics. It provides calculations
  of spectral densities, DC conductivity, and linear and nonlinear optical
  responses for large sparse Hamiltonians, with optional CUDA GPU acceleration.
keywords:
  - Julia
  - Kernel Polynomial Method
  - condensed matter physics
  - density of states
  - electronic transport
  - optical response
  - GPU acceleration
